--
N5008 [stmt.if]/2: return type deduction took the FIRST return statement in
source order even when it sat in an `if constexpr` branch that is discarded
for the instantiation -- libstdc++'s views::all (`if constexpr
(view<decay_t<_Range>>) return std::forward<_Range>(__r); ... else return
ref_view{...}`) deduced `int*` for an array argument.  A return under an `if
constexpr` now defers deduction until the body is type-checked and the
discarded branch is gone.  Also [dcl.type.auto.deduct]/4: the deduced type
drops a reference and top-level cv-qualifiers (`return static_cast<R &&>(r)`
with R = int*& used to give the function the return type `int *&`).
Non-vacuous: the last assertion states a wrong
value and must FAIL.
